      "title": "Videographer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\n\nThe approximate base compensation range is posted, but the actual offer will reflect our total compensation and benefits package. The offer will be determined by a number of factors including the selected candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, FTE, number of months worked, as well as internal equity among our team . Qualifications The ideal candidate will be able to produce high-quality video content that is compelling, authentic, engaging and can distinguish St. Scholastica’s brand, programs, student experiences, events and Athletics Minimum one year of experience in marketing, communications, content creation, or creative role Intermediate photography experience Intermediate experience with video production and editing. Intermediate experience creating a variety of digital and print designs Experience using Adobe Creative Suite applications, including Photoshop, Premiere Pro, InDesign, and Illustrator Excellent writing, editing, and proofreading skills Can work well in a collaborative environment Ability to meet strict deadlines and manage multiple projects within assigned time frames Responsibilities This position will support the College’s efforts by producing a variety of digital content for web including graphics, photography and video Produce high-quality, relevant content for multiple digital channels including website, social media, email campaigns and more Collaborate with the MarComm team to determine appropriate visual elements to illustrate specific stories, campaigns and collateral Conduct interviews, photo and video shoots Create graphics and templates for social media and video content Produce and edit videos for a variety of platforms including our website, YouTube, Instagram and TikTok Communicate effectively with staff, faculty, students and community members Maintain an organized asset library and digital workspace   #Ll-JG1",
